          <p>
            The <strong>complementary color wheel</strong> isolates two colors located precisely 180 degrees apart. Because they contain no shared primary wavelengths, placing complementary colors adjacent to each other produces maximum visual vibration—a phenomenon discovered by French chemist Michel Eugène Chevreul known as <em>simultaneous contrast</em>.
          </p>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#222222] bg-[#f9fafb] dark:bg-[#121212] p-5 sm:p-6 space-y-4">
